
=== Epoxy / 3M K46 syntactic foam: compressive modulus vs volume fraction ===
Constituents: epoxy E=3000 MPa, nu=0.35, rho=1.18 g/cm3; K46 shell E=60 GPa, nu=0.21, true density 0.46 g/cm3 -> eta=0.9356 (wall volume fraction 0.181).
Model: HP Mori-Tanaka (primary) on Hashin's equivalent hollow-sphere particle; HP differential scheme as the second estimate; HS bounds as the rigorous envelope. Units MPa, g/cm3.

Self-checks:
  E(vf=0) = 3000.0000 MPa (matrix 3000 MPa) -> PASS
  rho(vf=0.4) = 0.8920 g/cm3 (rule of mixtures 0.8920, expected 0.892) -> PASS
  all HP-MT and HP-DS estimates inside HS bounds on vf in [0,0.6] -> PASS
  eta = 0.9356 in [0,1) and vf_max = 0.60 < RCP = 0.64 -> PASS

Trend (MPa unless noted):
